# Debug-channel build counter for the mobile app.
#
# Bump this for every debug APK published to the debug update channel. It is what makes an
# installed debug build see a newer one: the marketing version stays put while a debug line
# runs, so without this counter every debug APK cut from one release version looks identical
# to the installed one and no update is offered.
#
# It produces a fourth version component (0.4.14-beta.16) and the tag debug-v0.4.14-beta.16.
# Ignored by release builds and by Xcode.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT IN Version.xcconfig, and this file exists only because it was there once.
# scripts/release-metadata.sh finds a release bump by walking the commits that touch the
# *version file* and reading MARKETING_VERSION at each one - it does not require the value to
# have changed. A commit that only moved the debug counter was therefore read as the previous
# bump, and release notes are generated across previous_bump..current_bump, so every debug
# build published between two releases silently truncated the next release's notes to the
# commits after it. It had already happened: with the counter at 15, 0.5.0-beta's notes began
# at "chore: debug build 15" and omitted the entire Streamlined pass before it.
#
# NuvioZDesktop has kept its counter in DesktopDebugVersion.properties from the start for
# exactly this reason. A separate file cannot spring the trap.
DEBUG_BUILD=16
